    <glyph class="process" id="rx00428" orientation="vertical">
      <notes>
        <html:body>
          <html:p>reaction: rx00428</html:p>
          <html:p>type: transcriptional/translational activation</html:p>
          <html:p>mechanism: transcription</html:p>
          <html:p>evidence: Here we report that both SAR Deficient 1 (SARD1) and CBP60g are key regulators for ICS1 induction and SA synthesis. Both proteins are recruited to the promoter of ICS1 in response to pathogen infections, suggesting that they control SA synthesis by regulating ICS1 at the transcriptional level.</html:p>
        </html:body>
      </notes>
      <extension>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:sio="http://semanticscience.org/resource/">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="#rx00428">
              <bqbiol:is>
                <rdf:Bag>
                  <rdf:li rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/skm:rx00428" />
                </rdf:Bag>
              </bqbiol:is>
              <bqmodel:isDescribedBy>
                <rdf:Bag>
