      <notes>
        <html:body>
          <html:p>reaction: rx00584</html:p>
          <html:p>type: transcriptional/translational activation</html:p>
          <html:p>mechanism: translation</html:p>
          <html:p>evidence: Inside the infected cells, the viral RNA of potyvirids is uncoated and translated into polyproteins which are proteolytically processed by viral-encoded proteinases producing, in most cases, the following mature viral gene products: P1, the helper component proteinase (HCPro), P3, 6K1, CI, 6K2, NIa (VPg + Pro), NIb and CP. </html:p>
        </html:body>
      </notes>
