    <glyph class="process" id="rx00786" orientation="vertical">
      <notes>
        <html:body>
          <html:p>reaction: rx00786</html:p>
          <html:p>type: transcriptional/translational repression</html:p>
          <html:p>mechanism: transcription</html:p>
          <html:p>evidence: At cooler temperatures, ELF3 (as part of the evening complex) represses the expression of PIF4. As temperatures rise, a PrLD in ELF3 promotes its phase separation and the formation of liquid droplets, thus relieving the transcriptional repression of PIF4</html:p>
        </html:body>
      </notes>
      <extension>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:sio="http://semanticscience.org/resource/">
